			"widgets_values":[
				"A 4-view character reference sheet of a short, stout, enthusiastic chef in his 40s with a thick curled mustache, tall white chef hat, white double-breasted apron, rolled-up sleeves, exaggerated energetic expression. 3D animated cartoon style, CGI animated feature film quality, NOT photorealistic. Views: FULL BODY FRONT (mid-action pose), FULL BODY REAR, FRONT CLOSE-UP (excited grin), PROFILE CLOSE-UP (mid-shout/action expression). Neutral grey background, clean studio lighting, no text or watermarks. High quality, 4K, 16:9 ratio.\n\nPart 1 (0–7.5s)\n\nCreate a high-energy cinematic animated short with Pixar-inspired 3D feature-film quality, NOT photorealistic, fast comedic pacing, exaggerated motion blur on rapid actions.\n\nSET LAYOUT: Small cozy kitchen, stove fixed center-back, chopping counter fixed left side, plating counter fixed right side. Camera geography stays consistent into Part 2.\n\nCAMERA ANGLES:\n\nQUICK WHIP-PAN OPENING: chef bursts into frame, sleeves already rolling up\nRAPID CLOSE-UP CUTS: knife blurring through vegetables at superhuman speed, ingredients flying comedically into a bowl\nFAST TRACKING SHOT: chef darting between counter and stove, exaggerated speed lines trailing behind him\nOVERHEAD SHOT: pan sizzling, ingredients tossed in with a dramatic flourish\nQUICK CLOSE-UP: chef's face, wild determined grin, sweat flying comedically\n\nThe energetic chef bursts into his tiny kitchen and instantly explodes into motion — chopping vegetables in a blur, tossing ingredients into a sizzling pan, darting between counters with exaggerated speed lines trailing him, comedic superhuman cooking energy throughout.\n\nStyle: Pixar-inspired 3D animated feature-film quality, NOT photorealistic, vibrant warm kitchen lighting, exaggerated comedic speed, punchy fast cuts, 16:9 aspect ratio, approximately 7-8 seconds.\n\n Part 2 (7.5–12s)\n\nContinue seamlessly from the previous scene. Maintain the exact same chef, kitchen layout, and Pixar-inspired 3D animated feature-film quality, NOT photorealistic.\n\nCAMERA ANGLES:\n\nDRAMATIC LOW-ANGLE SHOT: pan flip with a flare of flame, ingredients airborne in slow-motion beat\nFAST SPIN SHOT (360-DEGREE): chef spinning to grab a plate, plating with rapid precise movements\nOVERHEAD FINAL PLATING SHOT: dish assembled in seconds, garnish dropped with a flourish\nSLOW-MOTION HERO SHOT: chef presenting the finished dish directly to camera, triumphant pose\nFREEZE-FRAME CLOSE-UP: chef's proud grinning face beside the finished dish\n\nThe chef flips the pan with a dramatic flame flare, spins to grab a plate, and plates the dish in a blur of precise motion, dropping a garnish with a flourish. He presents the finished dish directly to camera with a triumphant grin, striking a proud freeze-frame pose as the dish steams invitingly.\n\nStyle: Pixar-inspired 3D animated feature-film quality, NOT photorealistic, warm satisfying payoff lighting, big comedic finish, 16:9 aspect ratio, approximately 7-8 seconds."
			],
